---
// 6. THE CHAPTER BREAK — bleed 2 of 2.
// This is the page's structural pivot: everything above it is her own work,
// everything below it is the index. It carries the OPEN rhythm step, which is
// spent here and nowhere else, so it reads as a deliberate pause rather than
// one more block in the stack.
//
// Obsidian ground. Gold on Obsidian is 5.8:1; gold on Porcelain is 2.4:1 and
// on Cashmere 1.9:1, both of which fail even the 3:1 large-text floor, so the
// dark ground is what lets this stay the page's loudest gold moment.
---

<section class="pullquote" id="sec-quote">
  <div class="spread">
    <p class="col-body">&ldquo;Every decision is viewed through a larger lens: <em>Legacy</em>.&rdquo;</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Full viewport width by nature — a top-level section, never inside .spread.
     The OPEN step sits both outside and inside it. */
  .pullquote{
    margin: var(--vr-open) 0;
    padding: var(--vr-open) 0;
    background-color: var(--obsidian);
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(88% 72% at 78% 10%, rgba(175,140,92,0.13) 0%, rgba(175,140,92,0) 60%),
      radial-gradient(70% 60% at 6% 94%,  rgba(71,68,64,0.58) 0%, rgba(71,68,64,0) 62%);
  }

  /* GOLD — the page's largest accent. Quote tier: opsz 96, SOFT 40, WONK 1.
     WONK 1 in italic swaps in the flagged ball terminals on b, d, h, k, l,
     v and w. That flourish is the whole reason this tier exists. Axes
     unchanged by this pass. */
  .pullquote p{
    /* Narrow inside its column: the void to its right is what makes the block
       read as hung rather than centred. */
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variation-settings: var(--fx-quote);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 340;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 112px);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-align: left;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* The closing word carries the section; Porcelain against the gold gives
     the line an internal contrast step without introducing a sixth colour. */
  .pullquote em{
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--porcelain);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px){
    .pullquote p{ max-width: none; }
  }
</style>
